    "updated_at": "2021-01-25T19:59:32Z",
    "body": "The desired behavior seems analogous to the `preventCancel` and `preventAbort` options to `pipeTo()` and `pipeThrough()`.\r\n\r\nIIRC calling `reader.cancel()` will cause `promise2` to resolve with `done` set to `true`. Using the `AbortSignal` should probably cause it to reject with an `\"AbortError\"` `DOMException` instead since the stream isn't really \"done\".\r\n\r\nIf we added an `AbortSignal` parameter to `pull()` then it would make sense to signal it in this case, but only if there were no other reads queued.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
