    "updated_at": "2021-01-26T12:16:11Z",
    "body": "Generally sounds good. This is safe in terms of the locking semantics because we cannot release a lock while there is a pending read request. Maybe that is worth noting.\r\n\r\nIs there a practical use-case for aborting a read request which has subsequent read requests?",
