    "created_at": "2021-02-04T20:55:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-02-04T20:55:20Z",
    "body": "I haven't heard a sufficiently compelling use case for cancelling a single `read()` while leaving other reads pending.\r\n\r\nStrictly speaking, if a call to `read()` caused backpressure to be relieved, then cancelling the `read()` should cause backpressure to be re-established, but we have no mechanism to do that.\r\n\r\nThe fact that this makes byte streams into a special case worries me greatly.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
